These are the SESAME materials needed for the double-shell problem.  The Spiner EOS
tables (materials.sp5) are NOT distributed; generate them from the *.dat descriptors 
with
sesame2spiner (built alongside singularity-eos):

    ./sesame2spiner -s materials.sp5 *.dat

You will have to create a sesameFilesDir.txt that points sesame2spiner 
at the SESAME data directories.

Material -> SESAME id map (see doubleshell.py MATERIALS):
    al.dat    3720   Aluminum (ablator)
    au.dat    2705   Gold (gap liner)
    be.dat    2024   Beryllium (tamper)
    ch.dat    7592   CH / plastic (foam cushion, glue)
    dt.dat    1018   DT gas (LLNL)
    glass.dat 7387   Glass (fill tube)
    he.dat    5762   Helium (background; only used if not treated as ideal gas)
    mo.dat    3539   Molybdenum (alternate inner shell)
    w.dat     3541   Tungsten (inner shell)

Note: doubleshell.py initializes Helium as an IdealGas (material0), so he.dat is only
needed if you switch the background to a tabular EOS.
